//Problem Statement: Student Marks Analysis Using COBOL Intrinsic Functions
//Objective: To use COBOL intrinsic functions to find the maximum mark, minimum mark, and average of three student marks.

IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
PROGRAM-ID. INTRINSIC-FUNC.

DATA DIVISION.
WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.

01 WS-MARK1 PIC 9(3).
01 WS-MARK2 PIC 9(3).
01 WS-MARK3 PIC 9(3).

01 WS-HIGHEST PIC 9(3).
01 WS-LOWEST  PIC 9(3).
01 WS-AVERAGE PIC 9(3)V99.

PROCEDURE DIVISION.

    DISPLAY "ENTER THREE MARKS:"
    ACCEPT WS-MARK1
    ACCEPT WS-MARK2
    ACCEPT WS-MARK3

    COMPUTE WS-HIGHEST =
        FUNCTION MAX(WS-MARK1, WS-MARK2, WS-MARK3)

    COMPUTE WS-LOWEST =
        FUNCTION MIN(WS-MARK1, WS-MARK2, WS-MARK3)

    COMPUTE WS-AVERAGE =
        (WS-MARK1 + WS-MARK2 + WS-MARK3) / 3

    DISPLAY "HIGHEST MARK: " WS-HIGHEST
    DISPLAY "LOWEST MARK : " WS-LOWEST
    DISPLAY "AVERAGE     : " WS-AVERAGE

    STOP RUN.
